  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <p>Near the hilltop village of Mons, in the Var, the Pont de Mons is a still-low-key swimming spot on the Siagnole, where dogs are welcome on a leash.</p>

      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A still fairly low-key swimming spot on the Siagnole, below the hilltop village of Mons. The water is cool, with waist-deep stretches, and the atmosphere stays unspoilt thanks to the limited parking.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Parking is very limited (about 3 spaces) on the side of the road towards Mons; a path then goes down to the Pont de Mons. If it's full, the area around the Pont de Siagne, a bit further on, is a good alternative.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: get there early to find a parking space — it's a fairly well-kept secret, but it fills up fast in summer.</div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs allowed at the Pont de Mons?</h3>
      <p>Yes, dogs are welcome on a leash at this swimming spot.</p>
      <h3>Where can you park to reach the Pont de Mons?</h3>
      <p>Parking is very limited, about 3 spaces, on the side of the road towards Mons; if it's full, the area around the Pont de Siagne, a bit further on, is a good alternative.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Mons, perched above 800m altitude, offers a superb view over the gorges from the access road.</p>
